/goslingmanagment","html_url":"https://github.com/goslingmanagment","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/runs/35089508675/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/runs/35089508675/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/check-suites/95023517581","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/runs/35089508675/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/runs/35089508675/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/runs/35089508675/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goslingmanagment/core/actions/workflows/359416594","head_commit":{"id":"d0a726c4f5c45d509cb209985943b70fe69ca547","tree_id":"d2f9022ed9b4aae3978300a4d6bdbff41a16686c","message":"fix(fansly): consume a 422 media rejection as a target fact, proven per namespace by a resumable witness proof (Decision 355)\n\nari-1's purchase_history stream sat blocked from 2026-09-02 to 09-15 on\none media: Fansly answers its order history with HTTP 422\n{\"code\":99,\"details\":\"error getting account media\"} — a media the\naccount no longer holds. The lane treated only 404/410 as target-local;\na 422 fell through to the executor's \"any other 4xx parks the stream\"\nrule, a request-contract verdict applied to a one-target fact, and no\noperator path exists to lift a provider_bad_data block on this stream.\n\nWhich answers are target-local is now the classifier's decision on the\ndurable payload (404/410 terminal_missing, 422 terminal_rejected); the\nhandler consults it first and re-throws everything else unjournaled, so\nauth/429/5xx/400-drift keep their executor classification. The rejection\nis journaled with the parsed details and the redacted body verbatim.\n\nA streak of three rejections in one request namespace (single media vs\nbundle) must be proven target-local before that namespace spends another\ntarget: page one of a witness — a completed chain of the same kind whose\nnewest answer the provider served, newest first, up to five — is re-asked\nand validated. Served proves the contract; rejected with a member's\nstatus (or a malformed body) is a storm vote; a different status is the\nprovider telling entities apart, no vote. Every witness voted → the lane\njournals a storm verdict (purchase_history_contract_storm, raw-only,\ncarrying its run id) and throws purchase_history_rejection_storm, parked\nas provider_bad_data. The chunk budget is five requests, so the proof\nresumes across runs. With no usable witness the lane spends one target\nper UTC day as evidence, otherwise brings a target of a namespace not\nyet deferred forward and keeps its cadence; only with every namespace\ndeferred does it sleep — never \"runnable\" with nothing to do.\n\nNothing is stored in the cursor: each namespace's epoch — streak, proof\nattempt, storm record and verdict, owed retries — is derived from the\ntimeline of served pages, rejected pages, witness pages (journaled as\npurchase_history_contract_probe, canonicalized like purchase_history)\nand verdicts. The owner's unblock buys exactly one target of fresh\nevidence, and only when the executor's record of the run that declared\nthe verdict shows it blocked on it — an older block cannot vouch for a\nnewer verdict, a run in between cannot erase an unblock. A served page\nthen means the contract was repaired, and every epoch member still\nrejected once at its cursor is retried once, at that cursor, behind the\nwalk's continuations and ahead of fresh work (a later served answer\nsupersedes the rejection in the chain resolver; a second rejection\nsettles it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-16T03:23:20Z","author":{"name":"Dmitriy","email":"dmsrg399@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"Dmitriy","email":"dmsrg399@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1174940243,"node_id":"R_kgDORggqUw","name":"core","full_name":"goslingmanagment/core","private":true,"owner":{"login":"goslingmanagment","id":220680726,"node_id":"U_kgDODSdSFg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220680726?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment","html_url":"https://github.com/goslingmanagment","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goslingmanagment/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/goslingmanagment/core","description":null,"fork":false,"url":"https://api.githu